# Generated from the OSRS Wiki page "Transcript:Spirits of the Elid" by tools/quests/transcript_to_dialogue.py
0	section	Starting off
1	line	Awusah the Mayor	Many salutations to you. What brings you to our little town?
1	box	
1	select	Select an Option
1	option	I am an adventurer in search of quests.
2	line	Player	I am an adventurer in search of quests.
2	line	Awusah the Mayor	Hmm, well that could be quite fortuitous. We really could do with some help here. Our town seems to have come under a curse, and we are desperate to get it removed.
2	line	Player	A curse? What sort of curse?
2	line	Awusah the Mayor	Well first of all our fountain, which has served us for many years, suddenly dried up. We then started transporting water from the river, but what we carried would always have completely dried up by the time we
2	line	Awusah the Mayor	got it back to the village.
2	option	So what do you do for water now?
3	line	Player	So what do you do for water now?
3	line	Awusah the Mayor	Well it's tough. There is a guy who calls himself Ali the carter down in the market. He's from Pollnivneach, so the curse doesn't seem to have affected him. He's got a cart full of water which he's selling to the people here.
3	line	Awusah the Mayor	Unfortunately in typical Pollnivneach style he's taking the opportunity to sell the water at outrageous prices because he knows we are desperate. Oh and Rokuh has developed something quite remarkable, called a choc ice
3	line	Awusah the Mayor	which is helping people stay cool.
3	action	previous
2	option	Any idea how you got this curse?
3	line	Player	Any idea how you got this curse?
3	line	Awusah the Mayor	Well we think it was because we were negligent in our duty to protect a priest of Saradomin. He came to us a few weeks ago from the north and we welcomed him into our town. He taught us much of the wisdom of
3	line	Awusah the Mayor	Saradomin. Then about a week ago, we found him dead by the river. It seems unlikely that it is coincidence we were then cursed. If you look around the town you might be able to find out more.
3	select	Start the Spirits of the Elid quest?
3	option	Yes.
4	line	Player	Ok I will have a look around and see what I can do.
4	line	Awusah the Mayor	Good luck to you.
4	action	end
3	option	No.
4	line	Player	I'm sorry to hear of your plight, but I must be going.
4	action	end
2	option	I'm sorry to hear of your plight, but I must be going.
3	line	Player	I'm sorry to hear of your plight, but I must be going.
3	action	end
1	option	I'm just looking around.
2	line	Player	I'm just looking around.
2	line	Awusah the Mayor	Well we've not fallen on the best of times here, but there are a few shops to look around and we have someone selling a marvelous new invention called a choc ice..
2	line	Awusah the Mayor	Oh, and there's the old temple if you're interested in a bit of history.
2	action	end
1	option	I'm passing through on my way to Menaphos.
2	line	Player	I'm passing through on my way to Menaphos.
2	line	Awusah the Mayor	Oh you don't want to go there. I hear rumours of plagues and the like.
2	line	Player	Thanks for the warning, but I might go and investigate anyway.
2	action	end
0	section	Talking to Awusah after starting the quest
1	line	Awusah the Mayor	Many salutations to you sir, have you made any progress in uncovering the reasons for our curse yet?
1	select	Select an Option
1	option	I am working on it.
2	line	Player	I am working on it.
2	line	Awusah the Mayor	Please try your best, that water salesman is not doing much good for the economy of our town.
2	action	end
1	option	What was I meant to do again?
2	line	Player	What was I meant to do again?
2	line	Awusah the Mayor	Look around this town, see if you can uncover any information to why we were cursed and how the curse might be lifted. I suspect that it might be because a priest of Saradomin died while staying at our town, but
2	line	Awusah the Mayor	that isn't much help in getting the curse lifted and it is possible I'm wrong anyway.
2	action	end
1	option	I haven't really had the time to investigate.
2	line	Player	I haven't really had the time to investigate.
2	line	Awusah the Mayor	Well I hope somebody can find the time soon, the despair of the people of this town increases daily.
2	action	end
0	section	Talking to Ghaslor the Elder
1	line	Ghaslor the Elder	Good day to you young man.
1	select	Select an Option
1	option	I am trying to find out the cause of this town's curse.
2	line	Player	I am trying to find out the cause of this town's curse.
2	line	Ghaslor the Elder	Oh that's something which no one but the gods and the river spirits seem to know.
2	option	River spirits, what are they?
3	line	Player	River spirits, what are they?
3	line	Ghaslor the Elder	They're the guardians of the source of the river Elid, they'll know of our curse, seeing as it's related to water we bring from the river. It's said that nothing happens on the river that they don't know about.
3	line	Player	So would it be possible for me to find these spirits and ask them what is going on?
3	line	Ghaslor the Elder	Ahh now the spirits are something which no one from here have seen in a good long time, certainly not in my lifetime, I don't think even in my own grandfather's lifetime.
3	line	Ghaslor the Elder	Most the younger people of this town don't even remember that the spirits even exist.
3	line	Ghaslor the Elder	Here I have something around here somewhere which may be of interest to you.
3	line	Ghaslor the Elder	Aha yes here it is, the ballad of Jareesh. This tells of a previous quest to try and find the spirits.
3	box	Ghaslor hands you a scroll.
3	line	Player	Thank you very much for your help.
3	action	end
2	option	Thanks for your help.
3	line	Player	Thanks for your help.
3	action	end
1	option	How are things?
2	line	Player	How are things?
2	line	Ghaslor the Elder	Lousy, young people have no respect for their elders, there's too many confusing newfangled magic carpets and snake charmers around these days and now we don't even have any water.
2	line	Player	Well I hope things pick up for you.
2	action	end
0	section	Talking to Shiratti the Custodian
1	select	Select an Option
1	option	I am trying to find out the cause of this town's curse.
2	line	Player	I am trying to find out the cause of this town's curse.
2	line	Shiratti the Custodian	Well with the moral standards of this town lately, I'm hardly surprised.
2	line	Player	Why, what have they been up to?
2	line	Shiratti the Custodian	Nothing someone like you would understand.
2	action	end
1	option	Good day to you.
2	line	Player	Good day to you.
2	line	Shiratti the Custodian	Be Careful in here and don't touch anything! There's some old and valuable artefacts around here. Careless outsiders.. you're always coming in and making a mess of things!
2	line	Player	Ok calm down, I'm not going to touch anything.
2	line	Shiratti the Custodian	Yes, good don't.
2	action	end
1	option	What is this building?
2	line	Player	What is this building?
2	line	Shiratti the Custodian	This is our local shrine to She.
2	line	Player	What do you mean by She?
2	line	Shiratti the Custodian	Such ignorance! I suppose I should come to expect it. People are forgetting the old ways of the desert around here. But then.. What do those bureaucratic fools in Menaphos expect! If they're going to take so long to
2	line	Shiratti the Custodian	send us a new priestess of She. Do you know we haven't had one for five years now!
2	line	Player	Errm you still haven't told me what you mean by She.
2	line	Shiratti the Custodian	She! Otherwise know as Elidinis, Goddess of growth and fertility, Lady of the river, Wife of Tumeken, Flower of the desert, Mother of Icthlarin.
2	line	Player	That all sounds very confusing, I might just call her Elidinis for short.
2	action	end
1	option	What is that key on display?
2	line	Player	What is that key on display?
2	line	Shiratti the Custodian	That's a very valuable artefact. Keep your hands off it.
2	line	Player	..I just wanted to know what it did.
2	line	Shiratti the Custodian	That's the key to the holy chambers of the great and mighty Spirits of the Elid, and it's staying right there. There are other holy items about this building and keep your hands off them too, but most definitely keep your
2	line	Shiratti the Custodian	hands off the key. People already meddle too much with the affairs of the shrine.
2	action	end
