0	section	Talking to the Spirits of the Elid
1	line	Nirrie	What brings thee to our domain? It has been a long time since
1	line	Tirrie	we have seen any of your kind. Thou art not even
1	line	Hallak	one of the desert peoples!
1	select	Select an Option
1	option	Wow how do you finish each others sentences like that?
2	line	Player	Wow how do you finish each others sentences like that?
2	line	Nirrie	We are a gestalt entity. We each have our own body, but our minds
2	line	Tirrie	are united and we all think as one. Well except when Hallak doth leaveth
2	line	Nirrie	the toilet seat up.
2	line	Hallak	That's the way it's meant to be!
2	line	Nirrie	Ok we're a mostly gestalt entity. We each have own body, but
2	line	Hallak	our minds are united, except for some little parts which aren't. We mostly
2	line	Tirrie	think as one.
2	line	Player	That doesn't really have the same ring to it.
2	action	previous
1	option	Give Nardah its water back!
2	line	Player	Give Nardah its water back!
2	line	Nirrie	This little one doth come blundering into our abode making demands, with no thought for
2	line	Tirrie	diplomacy or decorum.
2	select	Select an Option
2	option	I come as an emissary from the people of Nardah
2	option	Who are you calling little?
3	line	Player	Who are you calling little?
3	line	Nirrie	You are little in power compared to us.
3	action	previous
2	option	Just tell me what it takes to get Nardah some water.
3	line	Player	Just tell me what it takes to get Nardah some water.
3	line	Tirrie	Thou shouldst calm down, getting worked up like that will not help thee.
3	select	Select an Option
3	option	I come as an emissary from the people of Nardah
3	option	Tell me what I need and I'll leave.
4	line	Player	Tell me what I need and I'll leave.
4	line	Tirrie	Well maybe we're not that desperate for thee to leave.
4	select	Select an Option
4	option	I come as an emissary from the people of Nardah
4	option	Look you don't want me to get annoyed.
5	line	Player	Look you don't want me to get annoyed.
5	line	Nirrie	That's a shame because thou art annoyed already.
5	select	Select an Option
5	option	I come as an emissary from the people of Nardah
5	option	Oh yes I'm annoyed, now give them their water.
6	line	Player	Oh yes I'm annoyed, now give them their water.
6	line	Nirrie	You know thou art really not skilled at diplomacy.
6	select	Select an Option
6	option	I come as an emissary from the people of Nardah
6	option	I haven't time for this nonsense.
5	option	I haven't time for this nonsense.
4	option	I haven't time for this nonsense.
3	option	I haven't time for this nonsense.
4	line	Player	I haven't time for this nonsense.
4	line	Nirrie	Well we know ye mortals are always in a rush with
4	line	Tirrie	your very busy little lives. We'd better let thee get on. We
4	line	Hallak	enjoyed thy visit.
4	action	end
1	option	Yes, it wasn't so easy getting in here.
2	line	Player	Yes, it wasn't so easy getting in here. Why have you made it so tough? You must really not like guests.
2	line	Nirrie	We are powerful spirits with direct contact to the great goddess Elidinis, we do not need to be bothered by the trifles of
2	line	Tirrie	each and every human. This way only those of much resource and intellect, may gain audience with us.
2	action	previous
1	option	I come as an emissary from the people of Nardah.
2	line	Player	I come as an emissary from the people of Nardah. Their fountain has dried up and water they bring from the river dries up. What advice can you give on this matter?
2	line	Nirrie	How unusual, that the one who would come unto us on this issue isn't even from Nardah. Yes, it was indeed we
2	line	Hallak	who have withheld their water from them.
2	line	Player	Was this due to the death of the Saradominist priest as the towns people think?
2	line	Nirrie	No that also was our doing!
2	line	Hallak	He did not respect our ways and the ways of the desert! He did not respect the ways of Elidinis!
2	line	Nirrie	He came preaching the ways of Saradomin. Which is all well and good, but he also did turneth them from the path of the desert gods, especially Elidinis. Elidinis is happy to share the worship of followers, indeed Elidinis
2	line	Nirrie	was allied with Saradomin many ages past. Saradominist mages even gave us those golems you met as a diplomatic gesture, so you can see we have been on good terms. However this is an outrage.
2	option	Is there anything they can do to get their fountain working again?
3	action	below
2	option	Hey you've stopped finishing each others sentences.
3	line	Player	Hey you've stopped finishing each others sentences!
3	line	Nirrie	That seems to be something which happens when we get emotional
3	line	Hallak	We are
3	line	Tirrie	calmer now though.
3	action	previous
2	option	Don't many other towns not follow Elidinis though?
3	line	Player	Don't many other towns not follow Elidinis though? Why pick on Nardah specifically?
3	line	Tirrie	This is the truth, but there is more to the story than that. The answers
3	line	Hallak	lie in the story of Nardarine. Wouldst thou likest to hear the telling of this tale? It is not a short one.
3	select	Select an Option
3	option	Yes I would like to hear this story.
4	line	Player	Yes I would like to hear this story.
4	line	Tirrie	Nardarine came from a town towards the north side of the desert which does not exist today. This was in the third age in the time thou callest
4	line	Hallak	the God Wars. Her town was once controlled by Saradomin, but there was a great battle there between Saradominist and Zamorakian forces which pretty much levelled the town
4	line	Nirrie	to the ground. Most of the human citizens perished. Nardarine had the wisdom to escape into the desert before the fighting got really serious and thus survived. However she found herself wandering lost and alone in
4	line	Tirrie	the desert. She prayed to Saradomin for help, but Saradomin was too concerned with the loss of a strategic outpost to worry about the fate of one small human. Nardarine had wandered towards the realm of
4	line	Hallak	the Menaphite God Pantheon. Elidinis heard the prayers of Nardarine, she took pity on the wandering human and came unto her with water. 'Oh great goddess' exclaimed Nardarine 'I wish not to be involved more in
4	line	Nirrie	the wars of the gods for they have caused me so much hardship already, I wish only for a quiet life somewhere'. Elidinis replied 'I will grant this unto thee on the condition that thou swearest to forever pay fealty and
4	line	Tirrie	homage to me and I grant this also unto thine descendents as long as they too will pay an oath of fealty and homage to me'. Nardarine said 'If you would grant me a safe home, with a
4	line	Hallak	supply of food and water, then I would surely do this for it is more than any other God would seem to do for me'. Then Elidinis made
4	line	Nirrie	a spring of water appear at Nardarines feet and brought stone from below the sand so that she
4	line	Tirrie	might have something to build with. She called forth camels which have many uses and taste good in kebabs. She then provided Nardarine with a statuette in her image to worship. Nardarine built up her home. Over
4	line	Hallak	time more refugees from the God Wars found Nardarine's home. Nardarine let them stay with her as long as they did make the same oath as her. Hence the town of Nardah was born and Nardarine lived the rest
4	line	Nirrie	of her days in the peacefulness that she craved. The oath was passed down the generations for many ages, but now seemeth to be forgotten. Now maybe thou canst see why we are not best pleased.
4	line	Player	That does make some sense.
4	line	Player	Is there anything they can do to get their fountain working again?
4	line	Nirrie	I do not know. The Saradominist priest persuaded the people of Nardah to throw away a statuette of Elidinis which was in the temple. As long as they do not have that image of Elidinis to pray to, then we must consider
4	line	Nirrie	them turned away from her and the curse shalt stand.
4	line	Player	Well that's all very interesting, I wonder what the people of Nardah will think of this.
4	action	end
3	option	Is there anything they can do to get their fountain working again?
4	action	above
1	option	What manner of beings are you?
2	line	Player	What manner of beings are you?
2	line	Nirrie	We are the spirits of the river Elid, many ages ago we used to be mindless wandering spirits, with little mind or purpose, we were here even in the first age. Then great Elidinis came to the desert and bound us to her
2	line	Nirrie	river, we've
2	line	Tirrie	become one with the river and over the centuries become full of the power of Elidinis that was in her river. We are now her trusted guardians of the Elid, we can control the river and anything which happens
2	line	Tirrie	near the river we know about.
2	option	Wow how do you finish each others sentences like that?
