0	section	The Crevice
0	section	Talking to Awusah the Mayor
1	line	Awusah the Mayor	Many salutations to you sir, have you made any progress in uncovering the reasons for our curse yet?
1	line	Player	Yes I have made some progress. It is the doing of the water spirits at the source of the river.
1	line	Awusah the Mayor	The Spirits of the Elid? I wasn't even sure if they weren't some old wives tale. Why would they do such a thing?
1	line	Player	Did you by any chance throw away a statuette of the goddess Elidinis recently?
1	line	Awusah the Mayor	Oh that old thing. Yeah, the priest of Saradomin said we should get rid of that. He said we should become followers of Saradomin, and therefore we wouldn't need it.
1	line	Player	Well the spirits killed him for imparting that piece of advice about the statuette.
1	line	Awusah the Mayor	Gasps!
1	line	Player	Apparently this town was brought about by Elidinis on the promise that its people would follow her. People here have been waning in their belief of Elidinis for a while now.
1	line	Player	It seems the casting away of the statue was the final straw.
1	line	Awusah the Mayor	Ohh that's not so good if only we hadn't thrown the statue away, we wouldn't have this water problem then. He was a very convincing priest though. He worked many wonders, for example if he prayed hard enough
1	line	Awusah the Mayor	he became impervious to arrows. The way of Saradomin did seem very appealing.
1	cond	If the player has at least 40 Prayer:
2	line	Player	Oh but that's easy, I can pray to protect myself from arrows too.
2	line	Awusah the Mayor	Then truly you are very powerful too!
2	action	continue
1	line	Player	Where did you throw the statuette?
1	line	Awusah the Mayor	Ohh there's a strange deep crevice in the desert to the west of here. We threw it down there. I don't know if it's lost forever or not.
1	line	Player	Well it's worth a look anyway.
1	line	Awusah the Mayor	If you could retrieve it for us we'll be very grateful. Even if it doesn't give us our water back, maybe it'll calm Shiratti down, she was not pleased at it being thrown away and she's been grumpy ever since.
1	action	end
