1	option	Not yet, but don't give up hope yet.
2	line	Player	Not yet, but don't give up hope yet.
2	line	Awusah the Mayor	Good luck, may Sarad.. errm I mean Elidinis guide you.
1	option	Where did you say you threw it again?
2	line	Player	Where did you say you threw it again?
2	line	Awusah the Mayor	In a deep crevice to the west of this village.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Shiratti the Custodian
1	line	Player	I'm told that a statuette was removed from this temple.
1	line	Shiratti the Custodian	Yes, that Saradominist priest brought a group of the villagers in here. Took it by force as far as I'm concerned. I'm not at all happy, standards have been slipping here for a while, but that was going too far.
1	line	Shiratti the Custodian	It's an insult to She!
1	line	Player	Who?
1	line	Shiratti the Custodian	She! Elidinis! Goddess of growth and fertility! Lady of the River, Wife of Tumeken, Flower of the Desert. Mother of Icthlarin!
1	line	Player	..Ah yes, that She. Well you're right, that would be an insult to Elidinis. In fact it seems that affront is what has brought the curse upon this village.
1	line	Shiratti the Custodian	Well you know I suspected that all along, but does anyone listen to me anymore? No! Well I'm impressed you've come to the same conclusion as me, maybe I underestimated you.
1	line	Player	Er, why didn't you tell me about your suspicions when I was asking around about the curse then?
1	line	Shiratti the Custodian	I have to apologise. We've already had one outsider around stirring trouble, which caused this whole mess in the first place. I feared that you were coming to force your ways on us.
1	line	Player	No I'm here to help.
1	line	Shiratti the Custodian	Well I'm grateful, anything you can do to find the statuette would be appreciated.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Ghaslor the Elder
1	line	Ghaslor the Elder	Good day to you young man.
1	line	Ghaslor the Elder	Any progress on uncovering the town's curse yet?
1	line	Player	Yes some actually. I managed to speak to the river spirits you told me about.
1	line	Ghaslor the Elder	You actually managed to find them? I'm impressed. As I say - no one has seen them in many many years.
1	line	Player	Yes the spirits told me that the town is cursed because you guys have thrown away a statuette to the goddess Elidinis.
1	line	Ghaslor the Elder	Ah yes I heard a group led by that Saradominist priest went into the shrine and removed the Statuette. It all seemed a bit unnecessary to me. Didn't realise it would curse us though.
1	line	Ghaslor the Elder	I have no idea what they did with it afterwards.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to the Genie
1	line	Genie	I am a mighty and powerful genie. Why do you come here? Speak now or I'll have to think of something exceedingly nasty to do to you.
1	select	Select an Option
2	option	I'm after a statue that was thrown down here.
2	line	Player	I'm after a statue that was thrown down here.
2	line	Genie	Ahh yes someone did drop a statue on my head recently. Very nice workmanship, looks quite old and valuable too. I'm surprised someone threw it away!
2	line	Genie	I have accepted it as a gift as they clearly respect my terrible powers. They seek to keep me at bay by giving me valuables.
2	option	Maybe I can make a deal for it?
3	line	Player	Maybe I can make a deal for the statuette?
3	line	Genie	Hmm a deal eh? I think we can come to some sort of arrangement. I'll give you the valuable statuette in return for, let me think ....
3	line	Genie	How about I give you the statue in exchange for the sole of the mayor of Nardah?
3	select	Select an Option
3	option	Isn't that a little harsh?
4	line	Player	Isn't that a little harsh?
4	line	Genie	I wouldn't have said so. It seems a perfectly reasonable thing to request to me. I can think of many things a lot worse I could have asked for.
4	action	previous
3	option	How am I meant to remove someone's soul?
4	line	Player	How am I meant to remove someone's soul?
4	line	Genie	Oh that's easy. In my experience soles are very easy to remove with just a knife.
4	action	previous
3	option	Ok I agree to the deal.
4	line	Player	Ok I agree to the deal.
4	action	end
3	option	No way am I agreeing to that.
4	line	Player	No way am I agreeing to that.
4	line	Genie	Ah well it's your loss. No sole, then no statuette.
4	action	end
2	option	I'm not sure they know you're down here.
3	line	Player	I'm not sure they know you're down here.
3	line	Genie	Silence cur! They fear and respect me and that's an end to it.
3	line	Player	Maybe I can make a deal for the statuette?
3	action	above
1	option	You're a genie, grant me a wish.
2	line	Player	You're a genie, grant me a wish.
2	line	Genie	Not all genies are goody two shoes who go round granting wishes. It's something that my pathetic brother does to make people like him, but that's not my style.
2	line	Genie	I like to think of myself more as an evil and scary sort of genie, who people talk about in hushed and fearful tones.
2	select	Select an Option
2	option	Well you seem quite scary.
3	line	Player	Well you seem quite scary.
3	line	Genie	Why thank you, I put a lot of effort into my terrifyingness.
3	line	Genie	Wait! Did you say quite scary? I'll have you know I am VERY scary!
3	line	Player	Erm yes that's what I meant.
3	action	previous
2	option	I'm after a statue that was thrown down here.
3	action	above
2	option	Why are you sitting here in the dark.
3	action	below
2	option	Well I must be off now.
3	line	Player	Well I must be off now.
3	line	Genie	Yes, run. Ruuuun in fear of.. The crevice genie of Nardah! Muhahaha!
3	action	end
1	option	Why are you sitting here in the dark?
2	line	Player	Why are you sitting here in the dark?
2	line	Genie	Two reasons really. Firstly, I can see in the dark, so light or dark makes little difference to me.
2	line	Genie	Lastly, I gather it's normal for powerful terrifying creatures to lurk around in dark caves, so I found this one to lurk in myself, nice isn't it?
2	option	Very pleasant, the snakes are a nice touch.
3	line	Player	Very pleasant, the snakes are a nice touch.
3	line	Genie	Why do I get the sense that I'm not being taken seriously here? Please try to remember I am very dangerous and not to be trifled with.
3	action	previous
2	option	I'm after a statue that was thrown down here.
3	action	above
2	option	You're a genie, grant me a wish.
3	action	above
2	option	Well I must be off now.
3	action	above
1	option	I'm just looking around.
2	line	Player	I'm just looking around.
2	line	Genie	I don't know about that. I can't have just anybody traipsing in here. I have a reputation to keep you see.
2	line	Genie	Actually I'll tell you what, you can hang around here for a bit, but be sure to spread the word about what a terrifying experience you had when you ran into... The crevice genie of Nardah!
2	line	Player	...Ok I think I can manage that.
2	action	end
0	section	Talking to the Genie again after accepting his deal
1	line	Genie	Do you have the sole of Awusah, so that we can make our trade?
1	select	Select an Option
1	option	How am I meant to remove someone's soul?
2	action	above
1	option	I'm still working on it.
2	line	Player	I'm still working on it.
2	line	Genie	Well no rush, I quite like the statuette too.
1	option	No, it's not an easy thing to get.
2	line	Player	No, it's not an easy thing to get.
2	line	Genie	Haha, even a pathetic human should be able to manage to get another human's sole.
1	action	end
0	section	Sole Split
0	section	Talking to the mayor again
1	line	Awusah the Mayor	Have you had any luck retrieving our statuette yet?
1	line	Player	Err, well I have made some progress. I met a genie down the crevice. He told me that he would give me the statuette in exchange for your soul.
1	line	Awusah the Mayor	What! That's just asking to much. So, he want's to have my soul when my time to die comes?
1	line	Player	Well not exactly, he sort of basically said I should remove it with a knife.
1	line	Awusah the Mayor	That's barbaric! I simply refuse. The price is too high. We'll just have to find other ways to get the town a good supply of water. Don't go bringing any knives near me.
1	action	end
0	section	Using a knife on Awusah the Mayor
1	line	Awusah the Mayor	What do you think you are doing?
1	line	Player	Errm, I'm trying to remove your soul.
1	line	Awusah the Mayor	What, have you lost your mind?
1	line	Player	It's for the good of the village. I met a genie down the crevice. He told me that he would give me the statuette in exchange for your sole.
1	line	Awusah the Mayor	That's barbaric! We'll just have to find other ways to get the town a good supply of water. Keep your knife away from me please.
1	action	end
0	section	Attempting to cut the mayor's shoes in his presence
1	line	Awusah the Mayor	Hey, leave my shoes alone!
1	action	end
0	section	Cutting the mayor's shoes
1	box	You remove the soles from the shoes.
1	action	end
0	section	Returning to the genie with the mayor's "sole"
1	line	Genie	Do you have the sole of Awusah, so that we can make our trade?
1	line	Player	Yes I have it here.
1	line	Genie	Ah excellent, here's the statuette then.
1	box	You trade the sole for the statuette.
1	line	Player	So um, why do you need part of Awusah's footwear anyway? I hope you're not going to do some nasty magic on his feet or something.
1	line	Genie	I hadn't thought of that. I just read that a lot of the most powerful beings are collecting soles these days. I haven't really got many yet though. You provided me with an opportunity to expand my collection.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to the genie after losing the statuette
1	line	Player	I have lost my statuette.
1	line	Genie	Well fortunately for you, I am a mighty and powerful genie and managed to reacquire it. I will give it to you for another sole.
1	cond	If the player has a sole:
2	line	Player	Yes I have one here.
2	line	Genie	Ah excellent here's the statuette then.
2	box	You trade the sole for the statuette.
2	line	Genie	It's good doing business with you again.
2	action	end
1	cond	If the player does not have a sole:
2	line	Player	I will go and get one then.
2	line	Genie	Great! Another one for my collection.
2	action	end
0	section	Talking to the mayor with the statuette
1	line	Awusah the Mayor	Have you had any luck retrieving our statuette yet?
1	line	Player	Yes I finally got it. I had to destroy a pair of your shoes though. A crazy genie wanted a sole off your shoe in return for the statuette. I think he got souls and soles confused.
1	line	Awusah the Mayor	I suppose sacrificing a pair of shoes for the greater good of the town is reasonable. I don't begin to understand the ways of genies.
1	line	Player	Yes I thought it best not to correct him. He's somewhat less dangerous than he might be if he's a collector of shoe soles.
1	line	Awusah the Mayor	Anyway thanks for getting the statue back. You should take it to our temple and then we can see if our fountain starts working again.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Shiratti with the statuette
1	line	Player	I have got the statuette.
1	line	Shiratti the Custodian	That is great news! I could kiss you, but they don't allow shrine custodians to engage in that sort of behaviour. You should put the statuette back on its plinth.
1	action	end
